  "notes": "Mortality rates are printed as percentages (values_unit='percent') and must be divided by 100 to get decimal probabilities. The target blends Pre-Retirement and Post-Retirement rates. Post-Disability rates (page 107) are excluded from the blend as per instructions. The blend uses Active Member counts (Table A-5, page 78) for Pre-Retirement weights and Retired Member counts (Table A-26, page 90) for Post-Retirement weights. Active counts for '65 & up' are clipped to [65, 69] as active membership beyond 69 is negligible. Retired counts for 'Under 40' are clipped to [40, 44] (effectively 0 weight for ages <40) and 'Over 84' is clipped to [85, 89] for the purpose of the 5-year band mapping, though the source table has an open-ended bin. The source tables for rates (pages 106-107) list sample ages 20, 25, ..., 100. The row_map uses overlap_weighted to map these 5-year bands to single ages. Target ages 105-119 have no source data and are mapped to empty sources.",
